@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<h1>Privacy notice</h1>
<section class="panel">
    <h2>Who operates this service</h2>
    <p>The person or organization running this service (the operator) is responsible for how personal information is used here. Using Xenon does not make the software's author or contributors the operator.</p>
    <p>This notice explains how Xenon works. It is not a complete privacy policy for this service. The operator must also say who they are, how to contact them, their legal reasons for using personal information, how long they keep it, and which hosting and service providers they use. They must explain transfers to other countries where relevant and provide any other information required by law.</p>
    <h2>Sign-in and browser storage</h2>
    <p>Signing in uses Bluesky OAuth, which asks your account's services to confirm who you are and approve access. Xenon uses your verified account ID (DID), sign-in details and session information. Cookies keep you signed in and protect forms against requests made without your permission. The server's sign-in setup determines where access tokens and related information are stored and how long they are kept.</p>
    <p>These cookies are for sign-in and security, not advertising. Blocking or clearing them may stop sign-in or form submissions from working. Signing out ends your browser session, but does not delete moderation records or the audit log.</p>
    <p>Choosing Light or Dark saves that preference in this browser. Choosing System removes it and follows your device's appearance setting. Clearing browser storage also resets it. The preference is not saved to your account or shared with other devices.</p>
    <p>Your choice to display UTC or local time is also saved in this browser for later pages and visits. Clearing browser storage resets it to UTC. It is not shared with your account or other devices and does not change the times stored by the service.</p>
    <p>Media filter preferences are different: they are saved on this service against your verified account ID, so your blur, grayscale and translucent choices follow you across browsers. You can change them under Preferences in the account menu. They are not published as labels, shared with other moderators or sent to Bluesky. Operators and their storage providers may access stored information as part of running this service.</p>
    <h2>Moderation and administration records</h2>
    <p>The service uses and keeps team membership, permissions and status; reports and who submitted them; account IDs (DIDs), content addresses (AT URIs) and specific content versions (CIDs) when supplied; case assignments, notes, decisions and appeals; saved policies; label changes; and an audit log of reasons, times and tracking IDs.</p>
    <p>These records let the team review moderation, control access, recover interrupted work and account for its actions. Handles can change, so the service keeps account IDs to identify people and their actions.</p>
    <p>The server, services that forward requests to it, and logging or monitoring providers may also use information such as IP addresses, requested pages, times and error details. The operator must explain the logging and analytics actually used here. This notice does not promise that there is no additional tracking.</p>
    <h2>External services and disclosures</h2>
    <p>When you type a handle to add a team member, your browser sends the search text directly to Bluesky's public account-search service for suggestions. Bluesky sees that text and your browser's network information. These requests do not send your Xenon cookies, sign-in tokens or page address. You can also paste an account ID (DID) without requesting suggestions.</p>
    <p>Sign-in and account checks may contact Bluesky and other AT Protocol services, the account directory (PLC), and servers listed by an account's identity documents or handle. Checking content may contact the server that stores that account's data. Those services see the requesting server's network information and the account or content identifiers requested. Verified handles are saved temporarily to reduce repeated lookups.</p>
    <p>Opening a preview asks the public Bluesky content service (AppView) for the account or content and may fetch images from Bluesky's image servers (CDN). These requests come from this server without signing in to Bluesky. Bluesky sees the server's network information and the identifiers requested.</p>
    <p>Previews are displayed here without embedded third-party pages or your browser fetching remote images directly. Following a Bluesky link takes you to that external service. Previews show what is public now, not a saved copy of what was there when the report was submitted.</p>
    <p>Team members can see moderation and administration records only as their permissions allow. Hosting and storage providers may handle those records for the operator. The operator must explain any other sharing, including sharing required by law.</p>
    <p>If this service publishes labels, subscribers and anyone querying them can see the labeler, the account or content labeled, the label value, times and other information covered by the label's signature. Other services may keep copies. Public labels do not include report text or private case notes.</p>
    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>The operator's settings and obligations determine how long information is kept. Moderation history, audit logs, records of completed requests and backups may remain after you sign out or leave the team. Suspending or removing a member, withdrawing a label or closing a case does not necessarily delete these records or copies held by other services.</p>
    <p>Use the operator's published contact details for privacy questions or to ask to access, correct, limit the use of, or delete personal information, or exercise other rights provided by law. Some records may need to be kept for security, accountability or legal reasons. Where applicable, you can also contact the relevant data protection authority.</p>
    <p>Do not submit sensitive information that is not needed. If you cannot find the operator information you need to understand how this service uses your data, ask for it before submitting personal information.</p>
    <h2>Related information</h2>
    <p>Read the <a asp-area="Xenon" asp-page="/Terms">terms and conditions</a>, the operator's moderation policy and any additional privacy information. The operator must keep this information accurate and communicate important changes.</p>
</section>
